# ATS Mission Control & Simulation Overhaul Walkthrough

## Summary of Changes

### 1. Neural Model Expansion & Checkpoint Loading Bug Fix
- **Root Cause**: When [ContinualLearner](file:///c:/Users/Bob/Documents/github/ATS/mind/continual_learner.py) detected a learning plateau and expanded the policy hidden width (e.g. from 256 to 512), [`RLPolicy.expand()`](file:///c:/Users/Bob/Documents/github/ATS/model_rl.py#L89-L135) widened `fc1`, `fc2`, `actor`, and `critic`, but forgot to widen `self.embed_proj`. In `forward()`, `self.fc1(state_in)` was shape `[..., 512]` while `emb_feat` from `self.embed_proj` was `[..., 256]`, causing `RuntimeError: The size of tensor a (512) must match the size of tensor b (256) at non-singleton dimension 1`.
- **Fix**: Updated [`RLPolicy.expand()`](file:///c:/Users/Bob/Documents/github/ATS/model_rl.py#L89-L135) to properly expand `self.embed_proj` to `new_hidden_size` and copy learned weights.
- **Robust Loading**: Updated [`_load_policy()`](file:///c:/Users/Bob/Documents/github/ATS/main.py#L50-L70) and [`load_checkpoint()`](file:///c:/Users/Bob/Documents/github/ATS/model_rl.py#L150-L166) to dynamically inspect checkpoint `hidden_size` before initializing the network architecture.

